          "quote": "Since the grain refinement effect is more obvious at higher VED, according to the theory of Wagner [37], the critical concentration of external oxidation of active elements such as Cr and Al is greatly reduced by refining the grains. As a result, dense Cr2O3 and Al2O3 oxide films are formed, protecting the substrate and preventing it from further oxidation",
